#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Clinical SME, l1-extraction-reviewer, programme manager, business analyst, FHIR modeller, terminologist; the smart-guideline-end-to-end skill says which signs each stage. Each adjudication calls cat-harness's generic review (Process_Review) on the staged preview (feature-staging, staging-review) and records a qa-review/v1 Decision (approve, request-changes, reject) with the adjudicator's role id. A rejection files a bean against the stage and marks every asset derived from the rejected item rejected-upstream; it does not stop the agent."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:108
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Clinical SME: each source with why it was included or left out."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:95
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Component 1 sources of any DAK already in scope first, then WHO IRIS and the jurisdiction's own guidelines. Each candidate marked in-library / in-KG / not yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:236
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Decided on Task_L3Ready's ready: yes only when every L3 asset about to be written has an L2 asset upstream, every L2 asset an L1 node, and each review has been requested (opened and staged, verdict not awaited). No goes back to stage 4; a missing L1 extraction is stage 4's input gap, filled from stage 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:219
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "FHIR modeller and terminologist: one row per candidate IG, rejected ones included."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:27
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "From a use case to a consuming application: identify the L1 guidelines, ingest them into an L1 knowledge graph, choose the L2 DAKs to build on, create or adapt the L2 assets, choose the L3 IGs to build on, produce the L3 assets, then build the L4 consuming application the requester describes. Adjudication follows every stage as QA, not as a gate, but the order is strict: no L3 asset before the L1 extraction and L2 assets it derives from exist with their review requested (Gateway_L3Ready). Each stage forks into the next stage and its adjudication, and each adjudication has its own end event, so the instance completes only when all are recorded. Each stage runs the skill named on its activity, with its own input and output contract (l2-dak-authoring.bpmn for stage 4, dak-l3-ig.bpmn for stage 6), and its output is the next stage's input. The smart-guideline-end-to-end skill orchestrates the stages and says who adjudicates each."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:149
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "From the L1 KG: which existing DAKs to reuse, adapt, extend or reject, each with evidence and reason. Reuse first; prefer the jurisdiction's adaptation, recording the WHO original as its upstream. For each component kept, record how the candidate produces it (the tools graph, the candidate repository's source spreadsheets and converters, WHO's DAK toolchain); stage 4 uses that toolchain."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:63
#. Diagram label
msgid "Human adjudicators"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:203
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Index each candidate IG, then match the L1 KG and the L2 assets against it: reuse, adapt, extend or reject per IG, and record per artefact type the candidate's toolchain (CQL refresh, test-case format, example generator), which stage 6 then uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:235
#. Diagram label
msgid "L1 extraction and L2 assets exist, review requested?"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:135
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "l1-extraction-reviewer signs exclusions and coverage; Clinical SME reviews recommendations beside the printed page."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:308
#. Diagram label
msgid "L4 application built"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:337
#. Diagram label
msgid "no"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:192
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One review item per created or changed asset, shown as its reviewer reads it (diagram, table, data-dictionary rows); an adapted asset as a diff against its pinned upstream. Each form's wireframe candidates are reviewed blind and one is chosen (Process_Adjudication, Process_OptionsAnalysis). For each L2 component this is the review that forks inside its edit-and-review subprocess (l2-component-edit-review.bpmn), with the renderer, checker and reviewing role that skill tables."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:258
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One review item per created or changed resource: differential, each Questionnaire against the L2 wireframe it was derived from (field to item: fhir-harness fhir-questionnaire-wireframe, whose check is check-wireframe-questionnaire), CQL beside its DMN rule with test results, terminology expansions."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:121
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Per source not yet extracted: cat ingest into library/, the generic-document layer (l1-library), then the L1 layer (recommendations, remarks, practices, scenario candidates) into library/<bib>/l1-extraction/."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:87
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Population, setting, jurisdiction, interventions in scope. The user's own words; the agent asks a numbered question if the request did not say."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:164
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Programme manager and business analyst: one row per candidate DAK, rejected ones included."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:32
#. Diagram label
msgid "Requester (country team / implementer)"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:191
