msgid "Review each L2 asset (before / after if adapted)"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:257
#. Diagram label
msgid "Review each L3 asset (before / after if adapted)"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:40
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs every authoring stage with the skill named on each activity, and goes straight on once a stage's output exists and its review is requested. Adjudication runs beside it as QA; the order of stages is not optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:26
#. Diagram label
msgid "SMART Guideline end to end"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:83
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Someone needs a SMART Guideline, new or adapted, for a use case."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:173
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The authoring steps of l2-dak-authoring.bpmn (personas and scenarios, BPMN, DMN, data dictionary, indicators and requirements, terminology), plus the design of each data-entry form as wireframe candidates (wireframe-design-review, design use) from the persona, the user scenario and the core data elements. Its clinical validation is this stage's adjudication and does not hold up stage 5. The IG is built through fhir-harness's AST cache lifecycle (ig-ast-refresh.yml), with the DAK pre-processing as smart-base's pre-export overlay (dak-preprocessing, dak-pre-export.sh) and the DAK sidecars made from the AST (dak-postprocessing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:242
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The mapping and pipeline of dak-l3-ig.bpmn, up to a clean IG build. Every L3 asset names the L2 asset it implements in wasDerivedFrom, with that edge's adjudication state. Each Questionnaire is derived from the chosen L2 wireframe of its form. Publication continues in that process and is not on the path to stage 8."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:228
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The order rule as a check with its own contract (skill l3-readiness). Every source has its L1 extraction, every L2 asset names an L1 node, every L3 artefact about to be written names its L2 asset, and the review of each extraction and L2 asset has been requested. Returns ready and the findings, each with the stage that fixes it."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:33
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The person who wants the guideline and the application. Describes the use case (stage 0) and the consuming application (stage 7). The agent asks; it never invents either."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/smart-guideline-end-to-end.bpmn:278
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "To-be mode, from the stage-7 intent: two or more candidates, web and mobile, with real content from the L2 personas and scenarios. The agent goes on with its recommended candidate; the requester may choose another during adjudication."
msgstr ""

